00:29:12 UTC`, read 14 s later. **They agree** — no offset has to be applied when matching a DUT
log line to a host timestamp. Console driver timestamps in this log are the box's local clock
(NZDT, UTC+13); DUT log lines are UTC. So 13:4x NZDT = 00:4x UTC on the same date.

## Pre-run gate

Recorded in full in the campaign queue under "Gate record (group A)". In short: `tools/tb
precheck tb277 u2` → `/dev/u2` free, exit 5 for one FOUND item only, `ser2net` pid 744, the box's
own console daemon and the standing adjudication — not touched. The console was at an exec
prompt, not parked in config mode and not at a shell. No deployed `tb277.setup` exists on the box
(expected for this box; never bind one). The probe ran `--read-only` against the run `.setup` and
exited **2 NEEDS-CHECK** with two `CHECK_CABLE` lines on eth3 and eth4 — **both the known
read-only artefact** (the probe may not ping, so the box's MACs had aged out of the DUT's FDB)
and **both disproved immediately** by ping 4/4 on each leg. `bench-setup/tb277/bench-state.md`
was regenerated by the probe and restored with `git checkout --`; it is not committed. There is
no framework script in this group, so `pt_preflight.py` has nothing to check. The sentinel is the
parent session.

